# ── opero — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
config/api_keys.json
config/certs/
config/whatsapp_web/
                              # somebody your WhatsApp account, not just a key
**/token*.json
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/

# ── WhatsApp bridge runtime state ───────────────────────────────────────────
whatsapp_bridge/node_modules/
whatsapp_bridge/.wwebjs_auth/
whatsapp_bridge/qr.txt

# Local UI/runtime credentials and test state
ui/config/
whatsapp_bridge/.wwebjs_cache/
.pytest-tmp/
.test-tmp/

config/google_oauth_client.json
config/gmail_token.json
config/instagram.json

config/recovery/

# ── Local QA screenshots and vendored installer tooling ───────────────────────
future-ui-qa*.png
tools/nsis-*/

tools/ffmpeg/
